Create an ordered tutorial series Use an explicit Jinja list when a series must follow a fixed order instead of Flatmark's pagination sort order. In the series index page, define each entry and render the list: 
{{ '{%' }} set tutorials = [
    { "label": "Install the application", "url": "/tutorials/install.html" },
    { "label": "Create a project", "url": "/tutorials/create-project.html" },
    { "label": "Deploy the project", "url": "/tutorials/deploy.html" }
] %}

{{ '{%' }} for tutorial in tutorials %}
- [{{ '{{' }} tutorial.label }}]({{ '{{' }} tutorial.url }})
{{ '{%' }} endfor %}

 Set pagination.enabled to false in the page's front matter so the index is emitted as one page: ---
title: Tutorials
pagination:
  enabled: false
---
 The rendered links retain the order of the Jinja list.

Troubleshoot templates and tables of contents Content disappears from a template that uses extends When a Jinja template extends another template, put all child content inside blocks declared by the parent template. Content outside those blocks is not rendered. If _layouts/base.html declares this block: 
{{ '{%' }} block content %}{{ '{%' }} endblock %}

 Override that same block in the child template: 
{{ '{%' }} extends "base.html" %}

{{ '{%' }} block content %}
  {{ '{{' }} page.content }}
{{ '{%' }} endblock %}

 Do not add undeclared blocks to the child; the parent has no location in which to render them. A table of contents is empty in a content page Render page.toc from a layout or include, not directly from a Markdown content file. Flatmark creates the table of contents after it renders the Markdown headings, so the value is available during layout rendering. Place the table-of-contents markup in an include such as _includes/toc.html, then include it from the page layout. See the page.toc reference for its fields.

Search index When search.enabled is true, Flatmark writes _site/search/entries.json after rendering all content and index pages. The file contains a JSON array with one object per rendered page: [
  {
    "title": "Page title",
    "url": "/path/to/page.html",
    "text": "Rendered page text"
  }
]
 Field Type Description title string Value of the page's title front-matter key, or Untitled. url string Generated page URL, including base_url when configured. text string Plain text extracted from the rendered content before the layout is applied. Flatmark generates the index but does not define a query protocol. Search interfaces load and filter the JSON in the browser. If a search-results.html layout exists in the site or theme, Flatmark generates /search/results.html unless the site already supplies that output path. The default theme supplies the layout. See Enable site search for setup instructions.
